    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5503792/adjunct-faculty-sport-management": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Sport Management",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty – Sport Management Location Lawrenceville Job Type Part-Time Job Number Rider00416 Division Academic Affairs Department Management Opening Date 10/02/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit AAUP Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview The Department of Marketing & Management at Rider University seeks an adjunct instructor of Sport Management for the Spring semester beginning January 2027. This position is to teach Sport Management courses such as Introduction to the Business of Sports, Contemporary Issues in Sport Management, Economics of Sports, Business of Global Sport, Sports Analytics, and more. Successful applicants must be able to teach courses in person on the Rider campus; some classes are fully in-person and others are hybrid, with some in-person sessions required. Of immediate need is an instructor for Sports Analytics. This course addresses the theory, development, and application of analytics in sports. Analytics refers to the use of statistical techniques and visualizations to measure performance and make decisions. Students will learn about the application of analytics in sports for purposes of strategy, player performance, team management, sports operations and fantasy competitions. The Spring 2027 section of Sports Analytics will be offered on Tuesday evenings from 6:30-9:30pm in hybrid format with the option for some online sessions. Salary is $4,215.98 for a 3-credit course. Please note that a full course is considered to have 9 students enrolled in the course. If a section is not full, 8 or fewer enrollees, the salary is prorated based on the number of students enrolled in the course. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience A Master’s Degree or higher in Sport Management or closely related field, or equivalent professional experience in the sport management field. Demonstrated ability and experience teaching at the college level. Strong knowledge of sport management principles, practices, and contemporary issues in the sports industry. Commitment to fostering student success in both academic achievement and career development. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively with students, faculty, and staff. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Professional experience in sport management or a related field. Experience applying sports analytics principles within professional, collegiate, or amateur sport organization, sports media, or sports technology companies. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
