    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5494443/area-coordinator": {
      "title": "Area Coordinator",
      "description": "Area Coordinator Salary $49,800.00 Annually Location Lawrenceville Job Type Full-Time Job Number Rider00411 Division Enrollment Management Department Residence Life Opening Date 09/24/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for an Area Coordinator. Reporting to the Associate Director for Residential Education, the Area Coordinator (AC) is responsible and accountable for the day-to-day management of a residential area comprising multiple buildings and staff, including all aspects of residential learning initiatives, housing operations, and administrative functions. The AC will assume primary responsibility for supervision and evaluation of staff for their respective area; assist in the hiring and training of staff campus wide; oversee use of a learning outcomes framework for facilitation of residential environments consistent with the strategic goals of the University and the Division of Student Affairs; provide support for living-learning communities and affinity housing groups; coordinate operations functions including occupancy management functions, key control, maintenance work order tracking, and damage assessments and billing for their respective area; oversee and be an active participant in building prep activities prior to the start of each term; manage and oversee administrative functions associated with the residential area, including roster verification, room change processes, health and safety inspections, and roommate contracts; serve as a campus hearing officer within the student discipline system; collaborate with counseling, student health, public safety and other university departments for conflict mediation, and crisis intervention. As a generalist, the successful candidate must have demonstrated experience working in university residential settings; supervising paraprofessional/student staff; and coordinating housing operations functions. The AC will employ evidence-based best practices to implement and evaluate programs and services and maintain program effectiveness. The AC is expected to work collaboratively and develop productive working partnerships with multiple university departments. This is a live-on position, which requires the successful candidate to live in an assigned university apartment. The AC is required to participate in a 24/7 on-call rotation with other professional staff, remaining within a limited geographic range of the campus, and serving as a support for in-hall staff to respond to emergencies and facilities concerns that occur after normal business hours. This is a full time, 12-month position. Rider provides a generous tuition remission benefit to its employees to further their own education and, in many cases, their dependents' as well. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit Benefits | Rider University Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master’s Degree in Student Affairs, Student Personnel, Higher Education Administration or a closely related field. In lieu of a Master’s degree, a minimum of 3-5 years of full-time residential work experience in a Higher Education setting providing direct service to students, staff, parents and university partners will be taken into consideration. 2 years of experience in housing and residence life/residential education with direct experience providing supervision and training to paraprofessional staff. Experience implementing educational initiatives and overseeing living-learning communities in a college/university context as well as operations and live-in experience strongly preferred. Knowledge of housing occupancy management and operations. Demonstrated leadership ability, organization and planning skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality of sensitive information. Sensitivity to and ability to work with students, faculty, and staff of diverse backgrounds. Demonstrated ability to foster and maintain collaborative working relationships. Demonstrated ability to facilitate teams and groups. Knowledge of all laws likely to have an effect upon University students. Ability to work in a stressful and changing environment and with great attention to detail. Ability to handle multiple assignments and balance competing priorities and develop efficient work plans. Expertise in budget oversight. Strong analytical, and organization skills; excellent interpersonal skills; excellent oral and written communication skills; excellent training skills; strong conflict resolution skills; excellent program development skills. Ability to communicate effectively and interact tactfully with all levels of university students, staff, and faculty; read, analyze, and interpret documents, policies, budgets and contracts; and respond effectively to the most sensitive inquiries or complaints. Ability to define problems; collect and interpret data; and apply data and analysis skills to the formulation of proposals and solutions. Proficient in use of technology to carry out electronic communication and develop both printed and electronic documents using computers and the Internet. Experience with Windows system software, Microsoft Office (Excel, Microsoft Word, Power Point), Outlook and other e-mail software. Availability to work varied and flexible hours. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Live on campus position Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/full-time-administrative-employees Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5481719/assistant-director-of-housing-assignments-and-administrative-services": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Housing Assignments and Administrative Services",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Housing Assignments and Administrative Services Salary $56,000.00 Annually Location Lawrenceville Job Type Full-Time Job Number Rider00408 Division Enrollment Management Department Residence Life Opening Date 09/14/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for the position of Assistant Director of Housing Assignments and Administrative Services. Reporting to the Executive Director for Residential Engagement and Development, the Assistant Director of Housing Assignments and Administrative Services serves as a key leader within the Department of Residential Education and University Housing (REUH). This position is responsible for overseeing all housing assignment processes to ensure data accuracy and to maximize student satisfaction with the residential experience. Key Responsibilities: Support the management of the Cloud-based Housing Management System, StarRez. Through Cloud based computing, web services, and APIs, this position is responsible for database structures, report development, dashboards, and data analytics. Coordinate system implementations, upgrades, and modifications to maintain data integrity, collaborates with various support groups to enhance system performance and builds data schematics to make housing data accessible to other campus partners through data warehouse and dashboards. Manage and analyze housing occupancy data, prepare and disseminate reports, and develop and oversee marketing and promotional initiatives related to university housing services to support occupancy goals. Develop and maintain student meal plan processes and oversee the creation and ongoing management of content for the REUH website. Maintain strong collaborative relationships with campus partners, including the Office of Information Technologies, the Bursar’s Office, the University Registrar’s Office, Financial Aid, Student Accessibility and Support Services (SASS), Wellness Center, and other student affairs offices. Provide day-to-day oversight of departmental budgets and financial operations, supervise professional and/or support staff, and perform other duties as assigned. Serve in a campus-wide on-call capacity for emergency response. This position is a required live-in position. Rider provides a generous tuition remission benefit to its employees to further their own education and, in many cases, their dependents' as well. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit Benefits | Rider University This 12-month position includes a full benefits package, a furnished apartment on campus and a meal plan. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master's Degree in Student Personnel, Counseling, Higher Education Administration/Student Affairs, Public Administration, MBA or a related discipline. In lieu of a Master’s degree, a minimum of 3-5 years of full-time residential work experience in a Higher Education setting providing direct service to students, staff, parents and university partners will be taken into consideration. 2-5 years of related and progressively responsible experience in college/university housing with direct experience planning and coordinating housing assignments, room changes, and related processes. Experience supervising paraprofessional staff, using database technology to support housing services, and other computer skills appropriate to the position. Ability to work in a stressful environment and with great attention to detail. Demonstrated commitment to university programs, policies and services intended to maximize student personal growth, education and development. Demonstrated knowledge of current student affairs as well as university housing trends and issues. Demonstrated leadership ability and team orientation. Demonstrated success working within the university community. Sensitivity to the needs of a diverse student population and promoting a campus climate that encourages inclusion. Knowledge of all federal, state, and municipal laws likely to have an effect upon areas supervised, especially safety and risk management. Strong analytical and organization skills. Excellent interpersonal, cultural/intercultural, and community relations skills; excellent supervision, presentation, teaching, and training skills. Strong budgeting and financial planning/analysis skills. Strong problem solving and conflict resolution skills. Ability to communicate effectively and interact tactfully with all levels of university students, staff, faculty, and trustees; read, analyze, and interpret documents, budgets and contracts; and respond effectively to the most sensitive inquiries or complaints. Ability to define problems, collect and analyze data, conduct assessment of needs and program effectiveness, and apply data and analysis skills to the formulation of proposals and solutions. Proficient in use of technology to carry out electronic communication and develop both printed and electronic documents using computers and the Internet. Experience with housing database systems is required with a preference of StarRez experience. Experience with Windows or Macintosh system software, Microsoft Office (Excel, Microsoft Word, Power Point), Outlook and other e-mail software, and Banner (preferred). Understanding of relational database systems and ability to oversee maintenance of technology assets. Availability to work varied and flexible hours. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Live on campus position Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/full-time-administrative-employees Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5516380/assistant-director-of-one-stop-student-services": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of One Stop Student Services",
      "description": "Assistant Director of One Stop Student Services Salary $58,000.00 - $61,000.00 Annually Location Lawrenceville Job Type Full-Time Job Number Rider00422 Division Enrollment Management Department One Stop Services Opening Date 10/14/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for the Assistant Director of One Stop Student Services. This position oversees the daily operations of a centralized student services office that provides front-line support for Admissions, Financial Aid, Student Accounts, Registrar, and related enrollment services functions. The Assistant Director ensures efficient office operations, coordinates staff activities, supports service delivery, and serves as a primary resource for students, families, faculty, and staff regarding enrollment-related processes. This position balances supervisory, advisory, and cross training responsibilities with active involvement in daily operations, including customer service, office administration, workflow management, payment processing, and issue resolution. The Assistant Director works closely with Enrollment Management departments to promote consistent service standards and an exceptional student experience. Key Responsibilities: Coordinate daily operations of the One Stop Student Services Center and ensure appropriate staff coverage during business hours. Assist students, families, faculty, and staff with inquiries related to admission applications, financial aid, student accounts, registration, academic records, and enrollment services. Handle escalated customer service concerns and assist with resolving complex student issues. Monitor service queues, office traffic, email communications, and response times to ensure timely service. Oversee mail receipt, distribution, document imaging, scanning, and records management activities. Assist with data review and quality assurance efforts to support accurate student records and transactions. Coordinate cross-training initiatives to ensure operational flexibility and continuity of service. Develop and maintain training materials and procedural guides. Ensure staff remain informed of policy, procedure, and system changes. Collaborate with Enrollment Management offices to improve workflows and communications to enhance service delivery. Contribute to departmental initiatives that support enrollment and retention goals. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Bachelor's degree required. Minimum of three years of supervisory experience, including responsibility for staff performance management and employee development. Demonstrated knowledge of customer service operations, preferably within a higher education environment. Experience managing customer service operations in a high-volume environment. Strong leadership, conflict resolution, and employee coaching skills. Excellent organizational, analytical, and problem-solving abilities. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage competing priorities while maintaining a high level of service and operational effectiveness. Demonstrated commitment to student-centered service delivery. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master’s degree preferred. Experience working in a centralized One Stop or integrated customer service environment. Experience working in higher education or other learning environments. Experience with Banner Student, Banner Financial Aid, Banner Accounts Receivable, or comparable student information systems. Knowledge of federal financial aid regulations, student billing processes, academic records management, and FERPA requirements. Experience utilizing operational metrics, dashboards, and reporting tools to assess performance and improve service delivery. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/full-time-administrative-employees Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
