    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5461176/associate-director-of-transfer-enrollment": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Transfer Enrollment",
      "description": "Associate Director of Transfer Enrollment Salary $51,000.00 - $54,700.00 Annually Location Lawrenceville Job Type Full-Time Job Number Rider00396 Division Enrollment Management Department Admissions Opening Date 08/25/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Work Schedule 8:30 am - 5:00 pm, Monday - Friday, 37.5 hours. Occasional nights and weekends. Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for the Associate Director of Transfer Enrollment. Reporting to the Director of Transfer Enrollment, the Associate Director provides support of transfer students and supports the transfer team and the university as a whole in achieving its goals. Key Responsibilities: Manages a transfer recruitment territory of approximately 10 schools in Northern, NJ, which includes meeting with counselors and students and provide accurate and detailed information of all aspects about Rider to external customers. Makes data-driven decisions independently for assigned territory. Supervises one full-time transfer counselor. Assists with the management of transfer student workers - assists with hiring, training, event, and day-to-day scheduling for student workers. Assists with the implementation and coordination of all transfer related on-campus events and serves as the co-advisor to an engaged and award-winning Transfer Student Association. Assists with the development and execution of creating articulation agreements from community colleges to Rider to help improve student access and outcomes. This includes, but is not limited to, working with faculty from various colleges and departments, as well as working with the Director of Transfer Enrollment and University Marketing and Communications to determine how to best promote the partnerships. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Bachelor’s degree along with 3-5 years of experience at the two-year college in an advising or student services capacity or prior experience at the four-year level in working with transfers. Excellent communication skills, detail oriented, and well-versed in the transfer student experience. Previous experience working with transcripts & degree audits. Excellent interpersonal and time management skills and the ability to work independently. Valid driver's license in good standing and vehicle required or have reliable transportation to carry out travel requirements of the position. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master’s Degree Bi-lingual (Spanish) Experience with Slate CRM or other college CRMs Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/full-time-administrative-employees Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5483937/associate-director-scholarship-stewardship-annual-giving": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Scholarship Stewardship & Annual Giving",
      "description": "Associate Director, Scholarship Stewardship & Annual Giving Salary $50,000.00 - $55,100.00 Annually Location Lawrenceville Job Type Full-Time Job Number Rider00409 Division University Advancement Department Advancement Services Opening Date 09/15/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for the Associate Director for Stewardship & Annual Giving . Reporting to the Senior Director of Development, the Associate Director plays a key role in advancing Rider University's philanthropic mission by developing and implementing comprehensive donor stewardship strategies that foster meaningful engagement, inspire continued generosity, and strengthen long-term relationships with alumni, friends, corporations, and foundations. This position serves as the primary steward for scholarship donors while supporting broader Advancement stewardship initiatives, including donor recognition, impact reporting, and acknowledgment programs. Working collaboratively across University Advancement, Finance, Financial Aid, and University Marketing & Communications, the Associate Director ensures donors experience exceptional stewardship through timely, personalized communications and meaningful opportunities to see the impact of their philanthropy. The Associate Director also supports the Advancement Services team by serving as a backup for gift processing functions and assists with initiatives that promote annual giving, including stewardship and acknowledgment efforts for the Rider Fund. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Bachelor's degree Three to five years of experience in advancement, donor relations, stewardship, annual giving, advancement services, or a related field. Demonstrated experience managing donor relationships and implementing stewardship strategies. Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to produce high-quality donor correspondence and reports. Strong organizational, analytical, project management, and time management skills with exceptional attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting deadlines in a collaborative environment. Experience working with relational databases; proficiency with Raiser's Edge preferred. Experience with Banner is a plus. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office, particularly Excel and Word. Demonstrated understanding of confidentiality, data integrity, and ethical fundraising practices. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as part of the University Advancement team. Flexibility to attend occasional evening and weekend events. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/full-time-administrative-employees Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
