    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5324700/lifeguard": {
      "title": "Lifeguard",
      "description": "Lifeguard Salary $16.50 Hourly Location Lawrenceville Job Type Temporary Job Number Rider00337 Division Student Affairs Department Recreation Programs Opening Date 04/29/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Work Schedule As needed, which includes nights and weekends. Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for Lifeguards. Lifeguards are responsible for ensuring the safety of all patrons using the campus pool facilities by preventing and responding to emergencies. This position plays a key role in fostering a welcoming, inclusive, and safety-conscious environment within the Aquatics program at Rider University. This is a part-time, temporary position. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Ability to remain alert, act quickly, and follow established emergency procedures. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Must be punctual, reliable, and able to work flexible shifts, including early mornings, evenings, and weekends. Must hold current American Red Cross Lifeguarding with CPR/AED for the Professional Rescuer and First Aid certification (or equivalent). The successful candidate for this position will be subject to a pre-employment background check. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Prior lifeguarding experience in a college or community setting. Knowledge of pool chemicals, mechanical systems, or basic facility operations. Additional certifications such as Lifeguard Instructor (LGI) or Water Safety Instructor (WSI) are a plus. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5509564/office-specialist": {
      "title": "Office Specialist",
      "description": "Office Specialist Salary $20.79 Hourly Location Lawrenceville Job Type Full-Time Job Number Rider00417 Division Enrollment Management Department One Stop Services Opening Date 10/13/2026 Closing Date Continuous FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit AFSCME Work Schedule 8:30 am - 5:00 pm, Monday through Thursday. 8:30 am - 3:30 pm, Friday. 36 Hours Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University’s One Stop Services seeks two Office Specialists who will serve as a primary point of contact for student administrative support within a coordinated, cross-functional service environment. This position provides accurate, timely, and consistent assistance to students across Financial Aid, Student Accounts/Bursar, Registrar, and Enrollment Operations functions through a unified service delivery model. The role is responsible for addressing routine student inquiries, providing guidance on established processes, and ensuring appropriate referral or escalation of complex, regulated, or policy-driven matters to designated functional offices. This position supports the delivery of a consistent and accessible student service experience across multiple communication channels. Responsibilities include: Use University systems and databases to access student records, troubleshoot issues, verify account information across several offices, update student information, track detailed student interactions, and process requests. Collaborate with other University offices to ensure seamless student support and issue resolution. Use the multi-line telephone call center to manage both incoming and outgoing calls. Serve as the first point of contact for students, families, and visitors at the front desk, responding to inquiries via phone, Zoom drop in, email, and in-person, providing exceptional and professional customer service and maintaining confidentiality. Register students for courses including adds, drops and withdraws. Process electronic approvals for courses requiring permission and overrides. Process change of majors, minors, specializations (concentrations), and certificates. Assist prospective students as it relates to application requirements and completion, as well as when registering for events tours, and interviews. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience High school diploma or equivalent with minimum 2 years of related work experience in customer service. Excellent listening, problem-solving, and critical thinking skills to accurately interpret and respond to inquiries. Strong interpersonal and verbal/written communication skills with the ability to handle inquiries professionally and empathetically. Ability to work independently and prioritize workload. Ability to articulate One Stop policies and procedures in a way that is accessible and clear. Excellent time management to accomplish work objectives with the ability to multitask in a fast-paced environment while maintaining attention to detail. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and/or Google Suite and the ability to learn University-specific software systems. Experience working with diverse populations and a commitment to providing inclusive, student-centered service. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Knowledge of Banner SIS. Prior experience at a college or university. Ability to speak Spanish, American Sign Language, or use Braille. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/full-time-afscme-staff Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5190654/public-safety-officer-per-diem": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer (Per Diem)",
      "description": "Public Safety Officer (Per Diem) Salary $19.00 Hourly Location Lawrenceville Job Type Temporary Job Number Rider00260 Division Student Affairs Department Public Safety Opening Date 01/07/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for per diem Public Safety Officers within the Office of Public Safety. The Public Safety Officer provides the university with excellent customer & community service assistance, protects life, and safeguards property through the maintenance of law and order by enforcing all rules and regulations governing Rider University. Responsibilities include: Conduct systematic patrols of buildings and the grounds to protect persons and property; Respond to any and all assignments and calls for service; Conduct traffic control functions, regulate parking in designated lots, issue parking permits, issue violation summonses and warnings, and perform vehicle registration; Promptly respond to alarms, determine the cause, advise the supervisor, and document the incident; Respond to emergency situations, evaluate and request assistance if needed; provide immediate care, advise the supervisor, and document with a report; Provide security services for various University and student social events; and Alert Facilities Management of systems fail. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience High school diploma or equivalent. Minimum of one-year law enforcement, security, military, or firefighting experience or a Bachelor's degree in a related field. Must be at least 21 years of age. Must have, or be willing to obtain within one year, CPR and First Aid certification. Must possess the following: demonstrated ability to work well with others and under both direct and indirect supervision; excellent interpersonal skills; demonstrated ability to be professional and calm under pressure; a high degree of dedication, honesty, and integrity; computer literacy; ability to perform physical aspects of the job; and willingness and ability to work flexible hour. The completion of a satisfactory background is required. Individuals must possess a valid and satisfactory driver's license. This position has been deemed essential by the University to ensure the continuation of critical University operations, attend to the needs of students and others, and protect the University's assets during an emergency or when the University has closed or suspended operations. University employees designated as essential personnel must remain on duty or report to work as regularly scheduled to avoid interruption of essential services unless directed or permitted to do otherwise, as indicated by their department supervisor. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience College degree and a minimum of two years security training with police training preferred. First responder or EMT certification Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5399894/sales-representative-student-media-center": {
      "title": "Sales Representative - Student Media Center",
      "description": "Sales Representative - Student Media Center Salary See Position Description Location Lawrenceville Job Type Part-Time Job Number Rider00375 Division Academic Affairs Department Radio Station, WRRC Opening Date 07/24/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview The Sales Representative for the Student Media Center at Rider University will be primarily responsible for generating sales leads, building relationships with a local and regional customer base located in Mercer, Bucks and Burlington counties , and closing sales to earn commission-based income for 107.7 The Bronc, 107.7 The Bronc Retro, The Rider News and RUN-TV. Compensation: 100% commission-based. Commission rate: 20% on new and returning business. Payment is contingent upon receipt of collections . Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience 2+ years’ experience in media sales or a related field preferred Strong communication, negotiation, and interpersonal skills Self-motivated with a goal-oriented mindset Ability to work independently and manage time effectively High school diploma or equivalent required. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Bachelor’s degree preferred. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
