    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5498796/writing-studio-coordinator": {
      "title": "Writing Studio Coordinator",
      "description": "Writing Studio Coordinator Salary $25.00 Hourly Location Lawrenceville Job Type Part-Time Job Number Rider00414 Division Academic Affairs Department Academic Success Center Opening Date 09/29/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Work Schedule Works within the time frames of 8:30am - 5:00pm, Monday - Friday, 20 hours/week, but as the Academic Success Center provides services at night and on the weekends, flexibility in scheduling is required. Friday is a strong requirement for training purposes. Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for a part-time position of Writing Studio Coordinator. Reporting to the Director of the Academic Success Center, the Coordinator provides direct oversight of all forms of writing tutoring. This position is responsible for researching best practices in writing tutoring and for designing, implementing, coordinating, assessing and sustaining high quality professional and peer tutoring services in the Writing Studio. Responsibilities include: working with faculty and staff to determine the academic support needs of students in their courses, promoting the use of Academic Tutoring services to students and instructors, recruiting, hiring, training and supervising 10-15 undergraduate and graduate students, monitoring sessions, conducting new tutoring training, facilitating ongoing training as well as designing and conducting observations and evaluation of each service. This is a part-time, 10-month position. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Bachelor's Degree in English, Education, or Literacy Minimum of 3 years’ experience tutoring for writing in a college or university setting. Experience supervising student and/or professional tutors. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master's Degree in English, Education, or Literacy 5-10 years’ experience tutoring for writing and supervising peer and professional tutors in a college or university setting. Experience with academic support program design and assessment of student learning outcomes. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/part-time-non-bargaining-support-staff Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rideru/jobs/5519653/acting-assistant-professor-exercise-science": {
      "title": "Acting Assistant Professor – Exercise Science",
      "description": "Acting Assistant Professor – Exercise Science Salary $66,306.23 Annually Location Lawrenceville Job Type Full-Time Job Number Rider00425 Division Academic Affairs Department Health Sciences and Nursing Opening Date 10/16/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit AAUP Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview The Department of Natural and Health Sciences is recruiting for full-time appointment as Acting Assistant Professor in Exercise Science for the Spring 2027 semester. Appointments may be continued beyond the spring semester into the 2027-2028 academic year. Responsibilities for this position will include contributing to instruction of exercise science courses (e.g., Exercise Testing & Prescription, Organization and Administration in Exercise Science, Introduction to Health Professions, Kinesiology, or closely related courses in our exercise science major) as well as courses in the candidate’s specialty that align with departmental teaching needs, advising students, and providing value to the Department, College and University. Willingness to work collaboratively with other faculty and to mentor students from a wide range of disciplines, cultures and academic backgrounds is essential. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience PhD or other terminal degree and professional certifications (e.g., ACSM-EP, NSCA CSCS, CSCCa) in Exercise Physiology, Kinesiology, Strength and Conditioning or related field. Clinical doctorates (DAT, DPT, DOT) may be considered with appropriate experience. Candidates should have a demonstrated record of outstanding teaching of diverse populations of undergraduate students, as well as the ability to engage undergraduates in an active, independent research program. Preferred candidates will have post-doctoral or clinical experience, experience establishing and supervising internships/field placements/clinic experiences, and experience with program accreditation. Candidates who are ABD at the time of application may be considered. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/aaup-members Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply"
    }
  },
